Group sequential designs fix the maximum sample size and the spending of \(\alpha\) in advance. Some settings do not allow that:

online experiments that run until a decision is needed;
a study that may be extended when new funding arrives;
a living systematic review that is updated whenever a new trial is published.

Anytime-valid methods control the type I error at any stopping time, however it is chosen (Ramdas et al. 2023).

